%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 280c4326a059df94fabc20b6d7fee8dc, type: 3}
  m_Name: SCENE2Narration
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  heading: THE MANSION
  typingSpeed: 0.0825
  punctuationPause: 0.61
  voiceTextRatio: 0.95
  pauseGame: 1
  loadSceneOnEnd: 1
  sceneToLoad: SCENE3
  cutscene: {fileID: 0}
  startDialogueOnEnd: 0
  dialogueToStart: {fileID: 0}
  lines:
  - text: '[wave=0.25]Once every [item]25[/item] years[/wave], representatives from
      every major intelligent species gather at the private estate of [item][wave=0.5]Graex
      Vohnuns[/item][/wave] to renew their vows of peace and pitch new ideas, but
      this year is different.'
    image: {fileID: 0}
    autoProgress: 0
    autoProgressDelay: 2.5
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6ed79a49783984743b2def4c4350879f, type: 3}
  - text: It honors the [wave=0.2][item]100th[/wave][/item] anniversary of the [wave=0.2][shake=0.2]Concord[/wave][/shake],
      hence why a rumor is spreading that [wave][item]Graex[/wave][/item] is going
      to announce something of [shake=0.25]utmost importance[/shake] at dinner. Besides,
      a new sharp life-form has joined the [item]ITN[/item], said to have [shake=0.3]advanced
      from powered flight to interstellar probes in a [wave=0.25]single lifetime[/wave][/shake].
      For the first time, the summit welcomes a representative of the [danger][shake=0.35]human[/shake]
      race[/danger].
    image: {fileID: 0}
    autoProgress: 0
    autoProgressDelay: 2.5
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a06fb6182c2194044b340ad6098c569b, type: 3}
  - text: Before you stands the private estate of [item][wave=0.15]Graex Vohnuns[/item][/wave].
      A mansion large enough to make the word mansion feel rather inadequate. [shake=0.25]Tonight[/shake],
      somewhere behind those walls, sit [item]representatives[/item] of civilizations
      that have crossed stars, outlived empires, and shaped entire worlds. And now,
      somehow, you are among them.
    image: {fileID: 0}
    autoProgress: 0
    autoProgressDelay: 2.5
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 01101713f7b07304f9fe7e9f98d35018, type: 3}
  - text: You make your way toward the entrance, up a staircase clearly designed
      for something with much shorter legs than yours. The [shake=0.3]enormous[/shake]
      doors loom ahead, covered in carvings you cannot read and, frankly, are not
      [wave=0.25]entirely[/wave] convinced are writing. Before you can knock, there
      is a [wave=0.15]quiet[/wave] [danger]click[/danger].
    image: {fileID: 0}
    autoProgress: 0
    autoProgressDelay: 2.5
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e1b2cd96f6fe95646ac4271766b71526, type: 3}
  - text: The doors [wave=0.25][shake=0.2]swing[/shake] open[/wave]. On the other
      side stands a [item]small alien[/item], [wave=0.1]barely[/wave] reaching your
      chest. He is dressed [wave=0.2]immaculately[/wave], hands folded neatly behind
      his back, staring up at you with a [item]smile[/item] that is perhaps just
      a little [shake=0.25]too[/shake] enthusiastic. For [wave=0.25]several seconds[/wave],
      [danger]neither[/danger] of you says a word. His [item]smile[/item] [wave=0.2]grows
      wider[/wave].
    image: {fileID: 0}
    autoProgress: 0
    autoProgressDelay: 2.5
    voiceOver: {fileID: 8300000, guid: afd5fd236f8d02244902528a4abf3fc4, type: 3}
